BT /F1 10 Tf 28 666.6 Td (1. What is the primary focus of Occupational Health & Safety \(OHS\)?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 44 653.6 Td (Answer: Protecting employees from accidents, injuries, and harmful substances \227 Correct) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 28 634.6 Td (2. Which type of workplace hazard includes exposed wiring, wet floors, and excessive noise?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 44 621.6 Td (Answer: Physical hazards \227 Correct) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 28 602.6 Td (3. In the Hierarchy of Controls, which method is considered the MOST effective?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 44 589.6 Td (Answer: Elimination \227 Correct) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 28 570.6 Td (4. What does risk represent in workplace safety?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 44 557.6 Td (Answer: The likelihood that a hazard will cause harm if exposed \227 Correct) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 28 538.6 Td (5. Which of the following is an example of substitution in the Hierarchy of Controls?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 44 525.6 Td (Answer: Replacing solvent-based paint with water-based paint \227 Correct) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 28 506.6 Td (6. What type of hazard is associated with bad posture and repetitive motions?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 44 493.6 Td (Answer: Ergonomic hazards \227 Correct) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 28 474.6 Td (7. When should hazard identification happen in the workplace?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 44 461.6 Td (Answer: During design, before tasks, during tasks, on equipment changes, and during inspections \227 Correct) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 28 442.6 Td (8. What is the least effective level in the Hierarchy of Controls?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 44 429.6 Td (Answer: Personal Protective Equipment \(PPE\) \227 Correct) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 28 410.6 Td (9. Which benefit of OHS relates to employees missing less work?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 44 397.6 Td (Answer: Higher productivity \227 Correct) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 28 378.6 Td (10. What should you do if something seems wrong with machinery while operating it?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 44 365.6 Td (Answer: Stop the machine and get help \227 Correct) Tj ET
