BT /F1 10 Tf 28 666.6 Td (1. What is the main advantage of data as evidence over anecdotal evidence?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 44 653.6 Td (Answer: Data uses a large sample collected systematically \227 Correct) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 28 634.6 Td (2. In a data matrix, what does one row represent?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 44 621.6 Td (Answer: One observation or case \227 Correct) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 28 602.6 Td (3. Which type of study can establish causation?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 44 589.6 Td (Answer: Experiment with random assignment \227 Correct) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 28 570.6 Td (4. What was the main problem with the 1936 Literary Digest poll?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 44 557.6 Td (Answer: The sample was biased toward wealthier voters \227 Correct) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 28 538.6 Td (5. In stratified sampling, what do you do after dividing the population into strata?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 44 525.6 Td (Answer: Randomly sample within each stratum \227 Correct) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 28 506.6 Td (6. What is a placebo?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 44 493.6 Td (Answer: A fake treatment used as the control in medical studies \227 Correct) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 28 474.6 Td (7. Which variable type can take any value in a range and is usually measured?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 44 461.6 Td (Answer: Continuous numerical \227 Correct) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 28 442.6 Td (8. What does random assignment in experiments accomplish?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 44 429.6 Td (Answer: It balances other variables evenly across treatment groups \227 Correct) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 28 410.6 Td (9. In the Google Transparency Report example, what does each row in the data matrix represent?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 44 397.6 Td (Answer: One country \227 Correct) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 28 378.6 Td (10. What does voluntary response bias involve?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 44 365.6 Td (Answer: No random sample; only those with strong opinions opt in \227 Correct) Tj ET
