BT /F1 10 Tf 44 621.6 Td (Answer: numerical \227 Correct) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 28 602.6 Td (3. ___ evidence is a story from one or a few cases that may be true but has a tiny sample.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 44 589.6 Td (Answer: Anecdotal \227 Correct) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 28 570.6 Td (4. The principle of ___ means using a large enough sample or repeating the whole study for reliable results.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 44 557.6 Td (Answer: replication \227 Correct) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 28 538.6 Td (5. A ___ is a fake treatment like a sugar pill used as the control in medical studies.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 44 525.6 Td (Answer: placebo \227 Correct) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 28 506.6 Td (6. When two variables show a connection and one tends to change as the other changes, they are ___.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 44 493.6 Td (Answer: associated \227 Correct) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 28 474.6 Td (7. The ___ is the whole grid of rows and columns organizing observations and variables.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 44 461.6 Td (Answer: data matrix \227 Correct) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 28 442.6 Td (8. ___ bias occurs when a random sample is drawn but only a non-random slice replies.) Tj ET
